        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pavane/{size}/2406_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-01-31T18:31:31.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I've replayed this scenario a dozen times now and have never won. &nbsp;One time I was close, with the villian only having one HP at the end. &nbsp;Does anyone have any suggestions for this game: Plague Rat, Ra, Sleuth Wraith, Absolute Zero, and Megalopolis?</p><p>With only three heroes they all seem to be infected in five rounds or less. &nbsp;Most of the villain's damage dealing is not scaled to the number of heroes, so the damage received relative to the damage inflicted is high for a 3-hero team. &nbsp;The Plague Rat has so many HP that the heroes cannot inflict enough damage before they are disabled. &nbsp;Abosute Zero is especially frustrating because his setup time is so long that he has taken so much damage before he can start using the Isothermic Transducer that he can only rely on a Cold Snap and/or Impales to do any damage. &nbsp;Absolute Zero is more useful disabled.</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:46:21.760Z",
